  "decision": "Use the 5-province, 120-municipality, 22-city (21 component cities plus separately listed City of Lucena) crosswalk as the working CALABARZON administrative locality denominator, with PSA attribution and codes. The rendered detailed lists are explicitly dated 31 July 2025; quarterly PSA revisions through 3Q 2026 do not report CALABARZON municipality/city edits, and the latest region summary reports matching totals. The inaccessible 3Q workbook remains a verification limitation. Do not freeze the full CALABARZON research scope: its 158 waterbody leads, island coverage, shared waters, and waterbody identities/geometries remain incomplete.",
  "requiredFollowUps": [
    "When the PSA downloadable 3Q 2026 workbook/API is accessible, verify the 142 names/codes against that version and refresh the row-level capture hash.",
    "Reconcile all 158 waterbody leads and separately sourced additions against this locality denominator, including island units and shared waters; do not convert municipality associations into waterbody boundaries.",
    "Retain scopeFrozen=false until marine, brackish, inland-water, island, geometry, and source-derived waterbody coverage is reviewed."
  ],
  "nonClaims": [
    "PSGC localities are administrative/statistical identifiers, not fishing-ground or municipal-water polygons.",
    "This crosswalk does not prove that all named waters in CALABARZON have been inventoried, that every locality has fishing access, or that an unlisted fish is absent.",
    "Lucena's separate HUC statistical treatment is not a legal determination of city status or a province-boundary ruling.",
    "The 3Q 2026 workbook was not downloaded; the artifact uses rendered PSA directory tables and documented quarterly changes."
  ]
}
